## CQ-FDR-01
@group client, instance mods (421 jars)
@commands launch to the title screen; list `/proc/PID/fd` there
@pass "Sound engine started"; `[jar handles] closed N stale mod jar filesystems (N zip files)` with N about the mod jar count and the open count dropping by about N; no socket or pipe numbered 1024 or higher
@fails no `[jar handles]` line: FdReleaseMixin did not apply (grep latest.log); `layout check failed` or `unexpected securejarhandler layout`: securejarhandler changed, read section 2
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## CQ-FDR-02
@group client, instance mods
@commands Singleplayer, create or open a world, play 5 minutes (sounds, chat, JEI, one dimension change), F3+T once
@pass no native crash; latest.log has no `ClosedFileSystemException` or `ClosedChannelException`; mod textures and lang present after F3+T
@fails a ClosedFileSystemException names who still reads the discovery copy: exclude that jar in `StaleJarHandles`
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## CQ-FDR-03
@group client, `FdReleaseMixin` disabled (mixin config toggle or an old Common jar), 421 jars
@commands launch
@pass dies in window creation (`stack smashing detected` or SIGSEGV in libglfw.so): proves the fix is what keeps it alive
@fails reaches the title screen: the jar count fell below the limit, add jars until it dies
@draft no batch holds this row yet
